    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i checked the events and it doesn't say OOMKilled, but the status keeps cycling. i've looked at the config files again and they seem 100% correct. it's like something is just messing with the startup process or eating the config file before it can even read it. any idea why a file would just end abruptly like that during a container start?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If the logs are showing \"unexpected EOF\" despite the ConfigMap appearing correct, consider if the volume mount on the container is failing silently or if propagation delay is causing the container to start too early. Examine the container's entrypoint script to ensure it's waiting for the volume to be fully mounted before trying to read the configuration file. Alternatively, if the image builds configured environment variables, ensure those aren't overriding or corrupting the mounted file's readability.",
      "source": "target",
